# decision-2-option-c.pdc
#
# Supplementary I/O PDC for the decision-2-option-c overlay on the Icicle Kit
# baseline reference design (MPFS_ICICLE_KIT_BASE_DESIGN, MPFS250T).
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# The April 2 baseline P&R placed the dedicated XCVR reference clock macro
# instance for the PCIe block implicitly: the placer ran against a clean
# netlist and recorded its placement decision into the designer scratch file
# MPFS_ICICLE_KIT_BASE_DESIGN.nmatinit.pdc with -fixed false.
#
# When SmartDesign was regenerated on April 28 to overlay the new
# decision-2-option-c HLS (nv_pid_top with hardcoded outer + AXI inner sector
# clamp), the netlist hierarchy changed enough that Libero's place-and-route
# database no longer carried the implicit lock forward. P&R then aborted on
# the first dedicated transceiver port with PRPF_009 across all 20 seeds:
#
#   PRPF_009: Dedicated XCVR reference clock port(s) for instance
#   'CLOCKS_AND_RESETS_inst_0/PCIE_REF_CLK_0/PCIE_REF_CLK_0/I_IO'
#   must be placed and locked before running Place and Route.
#
# The constraint below makes the placement explicit and locked, matching the
# coordinates the April 2 placer chose. ICICLE_PCIE.pdc still pins the
# top-level REF_CLK_PAD_P/N ports (L19/L20); this file complements it by
# pinning the dedicated XCVR_REF_CLK macro the netlist instantiates inside
# CLOCKS_AND_RESETS_inst_0.
#
# Instance path verification
# --------------------------
# Path matches both the regenerated SmartDesign netlist
# (component/work/MPFS_ICICLE_KIT_BASE_DESIGN/MPFS_ICICLE_KIT_BASE_DESIGN.v
#  -> CLOCKS_AND_RESETS CLOCKS_AND_RESETS_inst_0
#     -> PCIE_REF_CLK PCIE_REF_CLK_0
#        -> I_IO)
# and the April 2 nmatinit.pdc entry at x=2468, y=236.
#
# Durability
# ----------
# This lock will remain valid as long as the SmartDesign hierarchy keeps the
# CLOCKS_AND_RESETS_inst_0/PCIE_REF_CLK_0/PCIE_REF_CLK_0 nesting and the IP
# component name stays "PCIE_REF_CLK". If the Clocks_And_Resets subsystem is
# ever reorganized, update the -inst_name path here. The PCIE_REF_CLK macro
# physically targets the same XCVR reference clock pad pair (REF_CLK_PAD_P/N
# = L19/L20 on the Icicle Kit), so the (x,y) coordinate is stable across
# overlays.

set_location \
    -inst_name CLOCKS_AND_RESETS_inst_0/PCIE_REF_CLK_0/PCIE_REF_CLK_0/I_IO \
    -fixed true \
    -x 2468 \
    -y 236
